%% # Scene 05 — analyzer error during sampling, needle left down (sampling point)
%% # One carrier, geometry of scene 01. While the sample is aspirated the analyzer
%% # goes into error leaving the needle in the tube: it sends Status (Error), the
%% # interface replies OK and keeps the carrier still. An operator performs a
%% # recovery (the needle goes back up); when the instrument is green again it
%% # sends Status (Ready), the interface replies OK and releases the carrier.
%% # Carrier flow: right to left, Pit-Lane above the Main-Lane.
%% # Coordinates are in a fixed 1920x1080 space (track panel: x 30..950, y 120..885).
%% geometry sampling
%% subtitle Single carrier — analyzer error with the needle down, operator recovery
sequenceDiagram
    participant IF as Interface
    participant AN as Analyzer
    participant DMX as DMX

    %% carrier id=C1 sid=SID-000123 route=main_in,pit,main_out

    %% caption 1 · Main-Lane | A carrier holding a sample tube travels along the Main-Lane towards the analyzer interface.
    %% at 2.2
    %% move C1 to sampling
    %% on antenna1 C1
    %% caption 2 · Diverted — Prepare — Sample Acquisition | The carrier is diverted into the Pit-Lane without stopping and the interface sends Prepare. The gate stops it on the sampling point: the interface sends Sample Acquisition.
    %% on antenna1 C1
    %% highlight nsd duration=2
    %% on antenna1
    IF->>AN: Prepare SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1
    AN-->>IF: OK SampleId=SID-000123
    %% on antenna2
    IF->>AN: Sample Acquisition SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1 OK C1
    AN->>DMX: Query SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1 Sample Acquisition C1
    %% for C1
    AN-->>IF: OK
    %% after 0.1 Query C1
    DMX-->>AN: Tests to perform SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1 OK C1
    %% caption 3 · Test query — Aspiration | After the reply to Prepare the analyzer has asked DMX (LIS) which tests to perform. Now its needle goes down into the tube and it starts aspirating.
    %% after 0.1 OK C1
    %% needle sp down
    %% after 0.1 OK C1
    %% duration 2.6
    Note over AN: Pipetting Analyzer - SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 1.7 needle sp
    %% caption 4 · Instrument error | During aspiration the analyzer goes into error, leaving the needle down in the tube. It immediately sends its status (Error) and Sample Complete. The interface replies OK to the status.
    %% after 1.7 needle sp
    %% status analyzer error
    %% after 1.7 needle sp
    %% for C1
    AN->>IF: Status State=Error
    AN->>IF: Sample Complete SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.3 Status C1
    %% for C1
    IF-->>AN: OK
    %% after 0.1 Sample Complete C1
    %% for C1
    IF-->>AN: OK
    %% after 2.1 Status C1
    %% caption 5 · Operator recovery | Sample Complete is not enough: with the analyzer in error the interface does not move the carrier: the needle is still in the tube. An operator walks to the instrument and performs a recovery: the needle is brought back up.
    %% after 2.1 Status C1
    %% duration 6
    Note over AN: Operator recovery
    %% after 2.1 Status C1
    %% operator analyzer duration=7
    %% after 4.6 Status C1
    %% needle sp up duration=1.2
    %% after 2.6
    %% caption 6 · Instrument ready | The instrument is green again: it sends its status (Ready) to the interface, which replies OK. Only now the carrier is released.
    %% after 2.6 needle sp
    %% status analyzer ready
    %% after 2.6 needle sp
    %% for C1
    AN->>IF: Status State=Ready
    %% after 0.2
    %% for C1
    IF-->>AN: OK
    %% after 1.5 Status C1
    %% status analyzer normal
    %% after 0.2 OK C1
    %% caption 7 · Carrier released — Release | The interface releases the carrier. As soon as it has left the interface module, the interface sends Release.
    %% after 1.9 Status C1
    %% pass sp
    %% on antenna3
    IF->>AN: Release SampleId=SID-000123
    %% after 0.1
    %% for C1
    AN-->>IF: OK
